<Project>
  <!--
    Central Package Management (CPM)
    All NuGet package versions are defined here for consistency.

    PACKAGE SELECTION CRITERIA:
    1. Must be free/open source (Apache 2.0, MIT, BSD, etc.)
    2. Must be actively maintained
    3. Prefer Microsoft/official packages where available
    4. Minimal footprint - only include what's truly needed

    BANNED PACKAGES (DO NOT ADD):
    - FluentAssertions (restrictive license)
    - MassTransit (restrictive license)
    - Moq (controversial maintainer)
    - Any package with "non-commercial only" license

    LAST UPDATED: 2026-07-10 (versions verified against upstream release feeds)
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <!--
      Transitive pinning lets the versions below override transitive
      dependencies. This is how we force the SQLitePCLRaw native SQLite
      package up to a patched build (see the SQLite section at the bottom).
    -->
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>true</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>

    <!--
      One property per "family" so a single edit (or Dependabot bump) moves
      every related package together and stays consistent.
    -->
    <OpenTelemetryVersion>1.16.0</OpenTelemetryVersion>
    <ExtensionsVersions>10.0.9</ExtensionsVersions>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Microsoft.Extensions.* - Core DI and hosting (MIT License) -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />

    <!-- SQLite - Official Microsoft package (MIT License) -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite" Version="$(ExtensionsVersions)" />

    <!-- OpenTelemetry - Official packages (Apache 2.0 License) -->
    <PackageVersion Include="OpenTelemetry" Version="$(OpenTelemetryVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.Console" Version="$(OpenTelemetryVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting" Version="$(OpenTelemetryVersion)" />
    <PackageVersion Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Runtime" Version="$(OpenTelemetryVersion)" />

    <!-- Testing - xUnit 3 (Apache 2.0 License) -->
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.v3" Version="3.2.2" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.1.5" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="18.8.1" />

    <!--
      =========================================================================
      SQLite native library - CVE-2025-6965 / GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q fix
      =========================================================================
      Microsoft.Data.Sqlite pulls in SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3 transitively.
      Up through the 2.1.x line that bundle depended on the native package
      'SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3', and every published 2.1.x build of that
      native package (<= 2.1.11) ships a SQLite older than 3.50.2, which is
      flagged by NU1903 (high severity, memory corruption in aggregate funcs).
      There is no 2.1.12 yet, so we cannot fix it by staying on the 2.x line.

      SQLitePCLRaw 3.0.x is API-compatible (no code changes in .core per the
      upstream 3.0 release notes) and REDEFINES bundle_e_sqlite3 as just two
      dependencies: SQLitePCLRaw.config.e_sqlite3 + SourceGear.sqlite3. The old
      vulnerable 'lib.e_sqlite3' package leaves the graph entirely, so the
      NU1903 warning disappears WITHOUT any audit suppression.

      Because transitive pinning is enabled above, pinning the bundle to 3.0.3
      pins the whole SQLitePCLRaw family, and pinning SourceGear.sqlite3 selects
      the SQLite build (3.53.3 here - far newer than the 3.50.2 CVE fix).

      The native base name is still 'e_sqlite3', so Microsoft.Data.Sqlite's
      Batteries_V2.Init() and self-contained single-file publish keep working
      unchanged.

      To roll back later (e.g. once Microsoft.Data.Sqlite references 3.x itself),
      delete these two lines. If a future 3.x ever regressed at runtime, the
      alternative stop-gap is a targeted audit suppression:
          <ItemGroup>
            <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q" />
          </ItemGroup>
      but the version pin below is the real fix and is preferred.
    -->
    <PackageVersion Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3" Version="3.0.3" />
    <PackageVersion Include="SourceGear.sqlite3" Version="3.53.3" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
